# TanStack Query Document Architecture

Replace manual `useState`/`useEffect` data fetching and hardcoded mock data with a proper TanStack Query server-state layer for documents.

## Audit Summary

| Issue | Location | Problem |
|-------|----------|---------|
| Server state in `useState` | [data-library.tsx](file:///home/krishna/projects/otis/frontend/otis-ui/src/pages/data-library.tsx#L38) | [documents](file:///home/krishna/projects/otis/frontend/otis-ui/src/components/features/documents) stored via `useState` + `useEffect` → no caching, refetch on every mount |
| Manual upload side-effects | [data-library.tsx](file:///home/krishna/projects/otis/frontend/otis-ui/src/pages/data-library.tsx#L121-L152) | [uploadUserDocuments()](file:///home/krishna/projects/otis/frontend/otis-ui/src/api/docApi.ts#114-129) called directly, result manually prepended to local state |
| Manual delete side-effects | [data-library.tsx](file:///home/krishna/projects/otis/frontend/otis-ui/src/pages/data-library.tsx#L188-L214) | [deleteDocumentsFromProject()](file:///home/krishna/projects/otis/frontend/otis-ui/src/api/docApi.ts#65-75) called directly, manual state filter |
| Hardcoded mock data for mentions | [chat-page.tsx](file:///home/krishna/projects/otis/frontend/otis-ui/src/components/features/chat/chat-page.tsx#L57) | `MOCK_DOCUMENTS` used as mention trigger items — never real data |
| TanStack Query not installed | [package.json](file:///home/krishna/projects/otis/frontend/otis-ui/package.json) | Only `@tanstack/react-table` exists, no `@tanstack/react-query` |
| No QueryClientProvider | [main.tsx](file:///home/krishna/projects/otis/frontend/otis-ui/src/main.tsx) | Missing provider — must be added at app root |

---

## Proposed Changes

### Setup & Infrastructure

#### [NEW] [queryKeys.ts](file:///home/krishna/projects/otis/frontend/otis-ui/src/api/queryKeys.ts)

Centralized query key factory:

```typescript
export const queryKeys = {
  documents: {
    all: ["documents"] as const,
    detail: (docId: string) => ["documents", docId] as const,
  },
  chat: {
    all: ["chat"] as const,
    detail: (chatId: string) => ["chat", chatId] as const,
    messages: (chatId: string) => ["chat", chatId, "messages"] as const,
    attachments: (chatId: string) => ["chat", chatId, "attachments"] as const,
  },
};
```

#### [MODIFY] [main.tsx](file:///home/krishna/projects/otis/frontend/otis-ui/src/main.tsx)

Add `QueryClientProvider` wrapping the app (inside `AuthProvider`, outside `RouterProvider`). Include `ReactQueryDevtools` in dev mode.

